Al Qaeda affiliate JNIM has been intensifying its activities in Benin since 2022. The country serves as a transit corridor between the areas of operation of the group, which is well established in Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso. Two nature reserves have become logistical hubs for the jihadist fighters. Benin's army is striving to hold the line. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/140a90d0-ac2c-11f1-8e16-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-09-08-18h58m44s860.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/140a90d0-ac2c-11f1-8e16-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-09-08-18h58m44s860.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ed01ce8-ac27-11f1-8123-51e6e0840641</guid><pubDate>Wed, 09 Sep 2026 10:00:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenya cracks down on foreign traders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-cracks-down-on-foreign-traders</link><description>
